      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute closure remains a significant complication of percutaneous angioplasty, and coronary artery stenting serves as a useful bail-out device. We describe two cases of sequential implantation of dissimilar tandem stents, a Gianturco-Roubin (4 x 20mm) stent and a Palmaz-Schatz (4 x 15mm) stent, for long dissection complicating percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty."},
